Root freezes the exact argv before any run, for example: timeout --kill-after=2s 10s, then prlimit --cpu=10 --as=536870912 --fsize=2097152 --core=0, then bwrap --unshare-all --die-with-parent --new-session --ro-bind /usr /usr plus the bin/lib/lib64 symlinks --proc /proc --dev /dev --ro-bind <pinned input dir> /input --ro-bind <pinned 2-file packet dir> /packet --clearenv --setenv PATH/LANG/MHASH_PACKET_DIR=/packet, then python3 -I -B /input/test_script_hash_addendum.py -v.

Also required:
- capture stdout and stderr through bounded pipes;
- accept the run only with exit 1, empty stdout, 'Ran 14 tests', 'FAILED (failures=13)' with no 'errors=' and no other FAIL text;
- record the property as 'no persistent host writes', not 'read-only root'.

assessments.evidence:
Positive: the base slice is accepted in every T12 method (test:514, 520, 528).

Negatives, each constructed and pre-validated in T00 (test:205-217, 406-422):
- the UTF-8 BOM control is strict-valid UTF-8 beginning with U+FEFF;
- the 4 UTF-16/32 BOM controls round-trip with utf-16/utf-32 and are invalid UTF-8 (lead byte FF, FE, or 00 00 FE);
- the 4 no-BOM controls round-trip and are valid UTF-8 containing NUL;
- the 4 invalid-UTF-8 controls (C0 AF overlong, ED A0 80 encoded surrogate, E2 82 truncated, F4 90 80 80 above U+10FFFF) raise UnicodeDecodeError strictly and are otherwise well-formed, since they parse under errors='replace'.

Mutants killed: BOM stripping, json.loads(bytes) auto-detection (all 8 encodings and the BOM case), and replace/ignore/surrogateescape/latin-1 decoding. The checker refuses them in source: BOM at impl:121, strict decode at 125-130, and NUL-bearing text failing json at 133-140.

Residuals: the json-BOM-error mutant is behaviourally equivalent and survives; only the 2-byte overlong form is tested; the invisible literal at test:410 needs a byte check (F2, F7).

T15.1 (test:567-586): the positive script_hash('v2', CIP57_CODE) returns H. The 9 negatives are:
- plain _Str subclasses with valid content (an isinstance mutant would return the real hash, failing the expectation);
- tripwire str subclasses whose __eq__/__ne__/__hash__/__iter__/__getitem__/__contains__/__bytes__/encode/startswith/lower/strip/find/count/isascii raise TripwireError, which is not a ValueError, so use surfaces as an error, and any swallowed use is caught by log == [];
- __class__ impostors that are isinstance-true and type-false (test:273-278; CPython object_isinstance follows __class__);
- True as version or code;
- memoryview as code.

T15.2 (test:588-610): positives bytes(base) and the round-trip document. The 10 negatives are bytearray, memoryview, a _Bytes subclass, a tripwire bytes subclass, an impostor, None, and JSON true for plutusVersion, title, compiledCode and hash.

T00 proves construction and isinstance fire no hook (test:441-447). str/bytes __new__ consult only the plain argument. The checker refuses at impl:44, 64 and 117 before any content use, and its messages never format the input.

Residual F6: the exact-class and hook-ordering requirements are stricter than the literal D4 text. The JSON-true cases for plutusVersion and hash are weak discriminators.

Whole checker read line by line (impl:1-203):
- imports hashlib and json (20-21);
- 7 constants (24-31), 2 sibling classes (34-39) and 10 functions;
- attribute accesses limited to issuperset, fromhex, blake2b().hexdigest, startswith, decode, json.loads, add and append;
- no I/O, environment, clock, randomness, subprocess, getattr, dunder access, global rebinding or caching;
- definition-time annotation dict[str, str] only.

Effects are bounded: length first (66), 1 MiB (119), BOM (121), strict decode (125), parse_constant and the duplicate hook (133), ValueError and RecursionError mapped (137). Phase 1 then Phase 2, with fresh results (169-203).

Test loader (test:294-312): one bounded read; the same bytes are linted and executed via compile(tree) into a fresh ModuleType; exec globals get the full builtins (lint is not a sandbox, D1); no SourceFileLoader, no .pyc, no sys.modules or sys.path change. The lint is identical to the baseline (test:281-291 vs FROZEN:155-165).

No cache is written: the script is not cached, -B is set, and compile writes nothing. The test opens files only for reading, using fixed names under PACKET (test:118-120).

Source-only residuals:
- the UTF-8 decode ignores coding cookies (irrelevant to the 9070 B checker);
- linecache re-reads the test file during traceback display (and the checker at GREEN);
- stdlib .pyc reads under /usr (F4).

The proposed class (contract:186-199) matches the reviewed baseline class:
- timeout 10 s with kill-after 2 s; prlimit cpu 10, as 536870912, fsize 2097152, core 0;
- bwrap --unshare-all, including network, --die-with-parent, --new-session;
- read-only /usr, /input and /packet, plus /proc and /dev;
- --clearenv with PATH, LANG and MHASH_PACKET_DIR=/packet;
- python3 -I -B /input/test_script_hash_addendum.py -v.

-I also gives -E, -s and -P, so /input is not on sys.path and PYTHONINTMAXSTRDIGITS is ignored. /input holds exactly the test. /packet holds exactly CIP-0057.md and SOURCES.json, which are the only files the test reads. Modes are 0444 for files and 0555 for directories, with no implementation, cache, symlink or extra entries. Before and after pins and listings are taken. The invalidRED list (contract:168) covers T00 failures and errors, any error or other message, ImportError, crash, timeout, kill and extra entries. One attempt. The test imports no subprocess or network code and writes nothing.

The tmpfs root without --remount-ro is disclosed (contract:198), so I make no read-only-root claim; the property is 'no persistent host writes'. The absence of -S (site .pth files run) is disclosed.

Not disclosed, and required before any run (F4/F3/F1):
- an exact frozen argv with host bind sources;
- bounded pipe capture, because fsize does not bound pipes;
- a read-only record of the interpreter identity;
- lstat absence of any independent_script_hash.py entry;
- acceptance criteria: exit 1, empty stdout, no 'errors='.
